{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.BranchingGenericity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.BranchingGenericity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SchurPrincipalBranching","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlWeightLevelR"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlWeight_addCell_beyond_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlWeight_addCell_beyond_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L236-L255","doc":"**The one addable cell the `range r` sum omits carries weight zero.**\n\nA diagram with exactly `r` rows has an addable cell at row `r` — start a new row — and\n`sum_wenzlWeight_addCellOrSelf` sums only over rows `< r`, so that cell is missing from it.  It\ncontributes nothing: the resulting diagram has `r + 1` rows, and `wenzlWeight_eq_zero_iff` kills it.\n\nThis is what makes the guarded `range r` sum agree with a sum over the addable cells of `μ`, which\nis the indexing `MarkovNormalisation`'s `(λ, corner) ↔ (ν, addable)` reindexing uses.  Stated for any\nrow `a ≥ r`, since none of them can appear in the sum either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_wenzlWeight_addCellOrSelf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_wenzlWeight_addCellOrSelf","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L208-L234","doc":"**Branching for the normalised weight**: `∑_{a<r} w_{μ + □ at row a} = w_μ`.\n\nThe normalisation `w_μ = s_μ / [r]_Q^{|μ|}` is chosen so that the `[r]_Q` produced by\n`sum_schurPrincipal_addCellOrSelf` is exactly absorbed by the one extra cell each summand carries.\nThis is the \"weights are consistent under restriction\" half of \"these are the Ocneanu weights\" —\n`MarkovNormalisation.ocneanuWeight_addable_sum` at `r = 2`, now at every level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.card_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.card_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L200-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_schurPrincipal_addCellOrSelf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_schurPrincipal_addCellOrSelf","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L157-L198","doc":"**General-`r` branching for the corpus weight.**\n\n`∑_{a < r} s_{μ + □ at row a}(1, Q, …, Q^{r−1}) = (1 + Q + ⋯ + Q^{r−1}) · s_μ(1, Q, …, Q^{r−1})`,\n\nthe sum running over all `r` rows with the non-addable ones contributing `0`.\n\nThis is what #5575 proves at `r = 2` by way of `schurPrincipal_twoRow`'s telescoping closed form —\nnow at every level, for `QBeta.WenzlWeight.schurPrincipal` itself.  The single hypothesis `hgen` is\nthe same root-of-unity genericity `schurPrincipal_eq_zero_iff` carries; everything else is derived\nabove.\n\nThe summand is total (`addCellOrSelf` guarded by the decidable `IsAddableCell`) rather than indexed\nby addability proofs, which is what `qratio_prod_eq_zero_of_not_addable` buys: on a row that cannot\ntake a box the `q`-ratio is already zero, so the guarded sum and a sum over addable rows agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_ne_succ_of_addable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_ne_succ_of_addable","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L121-L153","doc":"**An addable row leaves a gap of two below it.**\n\nIf row `i` admits a box then `μ_i < μ_{i−1}`, so `β_{i−1} ≥ β_i + 2` — the row-length inequality and\nthe shift each contribute one.  Hence **no** other β equals `β_i + 1`: rows above are at least\n`β_i + 2`, rows below are strictly less than `β_i`.\n\n`betaR_lt` alone does not give this.  It says the β are strictly decreasing, which allows\n`β_{i−1} = β_i + 1`; ruling that out is exactly what addability buys, and it is what discharges the\n`hne` hypothesis of `QOU.Mathlib.sum_prod_qratio_weighted` — the hypothesis whose failure would make\na summand `0/0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.colLen_zero_addCell_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.colLen_zero_addCell_le","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L108-L119","doc":"**Adding a box does not raise the row count past `max(colLen 0, a+1)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_pow_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.betaR_pow_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L83-L106","doc":"**The nodes are distinct.**  `β` is strictly decreasing, and at a non-root-of-unity `Q` distinct\nexponents give distinct powers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hookProd_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hookProd_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L78-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.rowColProd_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.rowColProd_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L66-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.levelConst_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.levelConst_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L62-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.descFactF_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.descFactF_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L55-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.one_sub_pow_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.one_sub_pow_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/BranchingGenericity.lean#L46-L53","doc":"**The primitive.**  At a non-root-of-unity `Q`, `1 − Qⁿ` vanishes only at `n = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}